  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\"><em>Digital Marketing Applications</em>, published by Peter Lang Verlag in 2019, has generated three citations since publication, with scholarly uptake beginning to emerge in 2023 and continuing into 2025. The work is held in academic library collections and addresses a field\u2014digital marketing technologies and applications\u2014that remains active in marketing and business research.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This scholarly monograph examines digital marketing as a field of inquiry, tracing its origins, development, and technological foundations. The volume synthesizes perspectives from marketing and computer science to document emerging applications and trends in digital marketing practice and scholarship. As a foundational reference work on a rapidly evolving topic, it serves both pedagogical and research-oriented functions within marketing and business curricula.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Citation evidence reveals disciplinary engagement beginning several years after publication. Two citing works appeared in 2023: a bibliometric analysis of digital marketing research trends published in the <em>International Journal of Marketing Communication and New Media</em>, and a dissertation on multimodal genre analysis of online product information that engaged with the book's treatment of digital communication contexts. A third citation emerged in 2025 within a bibliometric study of search engine optimization decision-making strategies. The citing works span institutions across India and Malaysia, clustering primarily within educational sectors, suggesting the book has found adoption as a reference source in academic research and graduate scholarship.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Library data confirms modest but sustained teaching adoption. The work is catalogued in WorldCat under subject headings covering marketing, internet marketing, and social media, and holds representation in at least four library collections, indicating integration into institutional teaching environments. The book's conceptual scope\u2014spanning computer science, business, and marketing\u2014positions it as a cross-disciplinary resource suitable for programs addressing digital business strategy and marketing technology.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citation trajectory is early in character. With three recorded citations distributed across distinct citing works and venues, the record shows emerging scholarly recognition rather than broad or sustained uptake. No social media events, news coverage, or public discourse signals are currently recorded. The evidence base is limited but consistent with a reference work whose impact unfolds gradually through academic citation chains and course adoption rather than immediate or high-volume visibility.</p>",
